    <desc>Open the menu and move around <app>Pano Terminal</app> with the keyboard.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Keyboard access</title>

<p>Most things in <app>Pano Terminal</app> can be done with the keyboard:</p>

  <terms>
    <item>
      <title><key>F10</key></title>
      <p>Opens the main menu. Use the arrow keys to move in it and
      <key>Enter</key> to select. In fullscreen, where the header bar is
      hidden, it opens the context menu of the terminal instead. Programs in the terminal, such as
      <app>mc</app>, may want this key; to give it to them, open the
      <gui>Preferences</gui> and turn off <gui>Accelerator Key (F10 by
      default)</gui> in the <gui>Keyboard Shortcuts</gui> group.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>F10</key></keyseq> or the menu key</title>
      <p>Opens the context menu of the terminal.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>Ctrl</key><key>P</key></keyseq></title>
      <p>Opens the <link xref="cmd-palette">command palette</link>, which finds
      any action by its name.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>Ctrl</key><key>L</key></keyseq></title>
      <p>Moves the focus to the tab list, when the
      <link xref="gs-tabs#tab-position">tabs are on the left or right</link>.</p>
    </item>
  </terms>

  <p>All shortcuts are listed in <link xref="adv-keyboard-shortcuts"/>.</p>

